notes               = "Untitled in source. The deer runs through this part of the book: the آهوان of an old carpet in the Alizadeh letter, the deer hunted on the plain in not-having. Here the poet is the deer, and asks the beloved for cover. ۱۳۶۸/۱۰/۱۹ is 19 Dey = 9 January 1990, resolved exactly. Imported as a draft with machine / lantern layers; ===translation=== left for Ben."
draft               = true

===persian===

از شبِ دو چشم تو
خورشید سر می‌زند...
و... سبزه‌زارِ عشق
گرم از نگاهِ تو...
غرق در آفتاب.
من آهوی شکسته‌دل زخمی توام
من را در سایه‌هایِ گیسویِ سبزَت
پناه ده...
۱۳۶۸/۱۰/۱۹

===machine===

Out of the night of your two eyes
the sun comes up...
and... the green meadow of love,
warm from your gaze...
drowned in sunlight.
I am your broken-hearted, wounded deer —
give me shelter
in the shadows of your green hair...
1368/10/19

===lantern===

Out of the night of your two eyes
the sun comes up...
and... the meadow of love,
warm from your gaze,
drowns in sunlight.
I am your broken-hearted, wounded deer —
shelter me
in the shadows of your green hair...

1368/10/19

